-- A QIIT sort has no expression-level eliminator: what it has is the
-- pair of eliminator lemmas its `data` item generated, and eliminating
-- a variable of one is APPLYING one (docs/NovaElaboration.txt,
-- In-place elimination). Parameters first, then one motive per SORT of
-- the signature, then a method per point constructor — η-expanded, so
-- each goal is stated at the constructor it belongs to rather than at
-- a Π type — then a coherence per equation constructor, then the
-- eliminee.
data [a : 𝕌] ( Bag : U
     ; nil : El Bag
     ; ins : a → El Bag → El Bag
     ; swp : (x : a) (y : a) (m : El Bag) → ins x (ins y m) ≡ ins y (ins x m) ∈ El Bag )

def sz : (a : 𝕌) → Bag a → ℕ ≔ λa. λm. ?goal
